; Valuation-commodity fixture (CLEANUP.md HOLD-3) — a plain USD portfolio that a
; handful of unrelated FX cross-rates used to flip into a foreign base, zeroing
; the whole report.
;
; The journal declares FOUR `P` directives. Only ONE of them prices anything
; that is actually held (`VTI` in `$`); the other three are exchange rates for
; currencies jotted down on a trip, none of which the portfolio touches. Ranking
; valuation targets by how OFTEN they appear makes `EUR` the base (3 votes vs 1),
; and no chain of prices connects `VTI` to `EUR` — so a $1,200.00 position
; reported `marketValue = 0`, `basis = null`, and an `unpriced VTI` warning.
;
; Verified against hledger 1.52 (which never picks a single base — it values each
; commodity in its own latest price target, so the cross-rates cannot interfere):
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/fx-cross-rates.journal bal --value=end,'$' -e 2026-07-16
;     → $1,200.00 assets:broker:vti, $800.00 assets:broker:cash
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/fx-cross-rates.journal bal --value=end -e 2026-07-16
;     → identical (VTI's own latest price is the `$` one)
;
; `D` is deliberately ABSENT here so the fixture exercises the engine's automatic
; choice; `fx-cross-rates-declared.journal` adds it.

account assets:broker:vti    ; type: A
account assets:broker:cash   ; type: A
account equity:opening       ; type: E

2026-01-01 opening balance
    assets:broker:cash    $2,000.00
    equity:opening

2026-01-05 buy VTI
    assets:broker:vti     10 VTI @ $120.00
    assets:broker:cash

; The only price that values a holding.
P 2026-06-30 VTI $120.00

; Three unrelated travel cross-rates. Nothing in the portfolio is denominated in
; any of them, and none of them reaches VTI.
P 2026-07-01 GBP 1.15 EUR
P 2026-07-02 CHF 1.15 EUR
P 2026-07-03 SEK 1.15 EUR
